<task id="094" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Upload collision: ask BEFORE the bytes move (pre-flight probe), and add "Use existing"</title>
    <phase>0c Secure Documents — upload path decomposition</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Touches the live upload path and the shipped collision dialog; a regression here silently restores data loss or breaks a working user choice.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified once re-scoped; the hard judgement (two options vs three, fail-closed default) was already settled and shipped.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <effort-reason>Brownfield against a path that changed twice in three days; the re-scope itself needs care.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares the upload client and the wizard collision UI with 076 and 093.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>076</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
    <origin>notes/plan-upload-path-decomposition-2026-08-31.md §3. Owner: "we do not want to silent fail (or fail at the end)", and "open a dialog with user option to either replace or rename/create new."</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>🔴 RE-SCOPE THIS BEFORE IMPLEMENTING. Most of the original 094 SHIPPED on 2026-09-02. Read what is already done before writing any code — implementing the plan note as written would rebuild working behaviour and risk regressing it.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack engineer.</role>

  <goal>The user is asked about a name collision BEFORE their bytes are uploaded, not after — and "Use existing" becomes available once 095 lands.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 **ALREADY DONE — do not rebuild:**

  - **Explicit `conflictBehavior` on the small-upload path** — `9c208a7f2`.
  - **Collision no longer overwrites.** Server default is now `Fail`, so a same-named file returns 409
    with the existing file UNTOUCHED — `93d5e673e`. This ended the data-loss bug where a collision
    silently replaced the stored bytes and the user saw a Dataverse 412 "Duplicate Record" AFTER the
    original content was already gone.
  - **Typed `UploadNameConflictError`** through the upload clients — `086b9e9ce`, consolidated onto
    `@spaarke/sdap-client` in `047c9df8d`.
  - **The two-option dialog** — `09025ab39`. **Keep both** (`rename`) / **Save as new version**
    (`replace`). Owner chose TWO options, not three. A retry re-runs the full pipeline for that one
    file and MERGES into the batch result. A pending conflict row renders above `SummaryStep`.
  - **The signal path**, both directions: `nameConflict` up (`FileUploadService` →
    `MultiFileUploadService` → `UploadFilesResult.errors[]` → `UploadProgress` →
    `OrchestratorFileProgress` → the row) and `conflictBehavior` down.

**WHAT ACTUALLY REMAINS:**

1. **The pre-flight existence probe.** Today the collision is discovered by ATTEMPTING the upload and
   catching the 409 — i.e. the user waits for the bytes to move and is asked at the end. That is the
   half of the owner's requirement still unmet ("or fail at the end"). It matters more now than when
   the note was written: the client-side 4 MiB ceiling was removed (`4044286a6`) and the real limit is
   250 MB, so "ask after the upload" can mean a very long wait before a question.

   The container is SERVER-resolved, so the client cannot look inside it — it must ask the server.
   ⚠️ **Check `DriveItemOperations.ListChildrenAsync` for reuse BEFORE adding an endpoint** (CLAUDE.md
   §11). A new endpoint needs the three-question justification.

   ⚠️ The probe is an OPTIMISATION, not the guarantee. The 409 path MUST remain — two users can race
   between probe and upload. Do not let the probe become the only check.

2. **"Use existing"** — a third option meaning "do not upload; link the existing document". Depends on
   **095** (the intersection entity), because it needs the document to be associable to a second
   record. Do NOT attempt it before 095.

⚠️ `UploadOperation` throws `UploadNameConflictError` on 409 **before** the generic failure. That
ordering is load-bearing for the dialog — do not reorder it.

⚠️ The shared client's failure translation handles TWO injected-fetch shapes (throwing vs returning);
see `requestOrThrow`. Any new probe call must go through it, or its failures will be untyped.</background>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/plan-upload-path-decomposition-2026-08-31.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.SdapClient/src/operations/UploadOperation.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.SdapClient/src/operations/httpFailure.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/document-upload/MultiFileUploadService.ts</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">🔴 RE-SCOPE. Verify at current HEAD exactly which of the above is already shipped, and narrow this task to what remains. Record the narrowed scope before writing code.</step>
    <step order="1">Decide probe vs reuse: can `ListChildrenAsync` answer "does this name exist in this container" without a new endpoint? Answer the §11 three questions either way.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire the probe ahead of the byte transfer, reusing the EXISTING dialog and its two options. Do not author a second dialog.</step>
    <step order="3">Keep the 409 path fully intact as the race-safe backstop; add a test proving a collision discovered ONLY at upload time still reaches the dialog.</step>
    <step order="4">"Use existing" — only if 095 has landed. Otherwise leave it out and say so.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If answering the probe requires a new BFF endpoint, surface the §11 justification for owner review before adding it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If 095 has not landed, do NOT implement "Use existing" — narrow the task and record why.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The collision dialog, the typed error, the retry-and-merge path and explicit `conflictBehavior` all exist and work.</existing>
    <extension>This adds only the pre-flight question and (later) a third option to the SAME dialog.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>With a 250 MB ceiling, a user can wait out a long upload only to be asked a question that could have been asked immediately. The data-loss half is already fixed, so this is a UX-completeness item, not a correctness one — scope it accordingly.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Pre-flight collision probe ahead of byte transfer</output>
    <output type="test">Collision discovered only at upload time still reaches the dialog</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A colliding name is detected and the user asked BEFORE the bytes are uploaded.</criterion>
    <criterion>The 409 path still works and still reaches the same dialog (race backstop) — asserted by test.</criterion>
    <criterion>No second collision dialog is authored; the shipped one is reused.</criterion>
    <criterion>Any new endpoint carries the §11 three-question justification, or none was added.</criterion>
    <criterion>"Use existing" is implemented only if 095 landed; otherwise its absence is recorded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>NOT STARTED. ⚠️ Scope is MUCH smaller than the plan note implies — see the background block.</notes>
</task>
